    "reason": "[ev-583967e3eaf6] and [ev-00743dabf3b0] say the removal covers the `-querier.engine.timeout` CLI flag, its corresponding YAML setting and the querier `query_timeout` YAML setting; [ev-dd7c1ff4a7b1] and [ev-cb9a7ce2cb5d] confirm this and point users to `limits_config`. So an exposure that only checks the CLI flag is too narrow: it misses environments that set the timeout in the YAML config. To express the YAML cases, I need to know which ConfigMap data key holds Loki's config or which Helm values path feeds `querier.engine.timeout` and `querier.query_timeout`, and the evidence doesn't say. A plain text-line match on `query_timeout` would also flag the `limits_config` replacement, so it can't be written precisely without that information.",
